  "description": "The Multi-Terrain Crossover MTX range of front suspension hybrids is incredibly versatile. Lightweight aluminium frames with stable and comfortable riding positions, broad gear ranges, powerful hydraulic disc brakes and short travel suspension forks mean these bikes can handle almost anything. Rough roads, cycle paths and off-road trails are all in a day’s work for an MTX.\n\nThe MTX 8.8 Women's offers a high performing specification blending comfort and efficiency in a well-rounded package. A female-specific saddle with handlebar width, stem and crank length sized to suite female riders ensure a comfortable ride. Shimano’s 2x10 speed Deore gears give a low ratio for climbing without compromising cruising speed, with small steps in between. A clutch mechanism in the rear derailleur helps stop dropping chains too. Shimano MT-200 hydraulic disc brakes are low-maintenance and stop quickly with easily modulated braking power.\n\nThe Schwalbe Tyrago 35mm tyres grip well on loose surfaces and still roll quickly, protecting you from punctures with a Kevlar breaker belt. Add in a Suntour NXC-D Air sprung suspension fork, mounts for mudguards and a pannier rack and there’s not a lot the MTX 8.8 can’t turn its hand to.\n\nHighlights\n\nLightweight triple-butted aluminium frame with comfortable ride position\n\nStable handling and lighter, air suspension fork for off road riding or rough roads\n\n35mm Schwalbe Tyrago puncture-resistant tyres\n\nFemale-specific saddle developed with industry experts with comfort in mind",
